          "path": "_m/g/c/p/v/holborn-tube-station-wp/holborn-tube-station-geograph-.jpg",
          "filename": "Holborn tube station - geograph.org.uk - 668972.jpg",
          "caption": "Holborn tube station Holborn is on both the Central and Piccadilly Lines, and the Piccadilly Line station was opened in 1906. In 1933 the station was substantially modernized including the opening of the Central Line station, which replaced the British Museum station about 250 metres away to the west. \nThis is the west entrance to the station in Kingsway. There is a north entrance in High Holborn round to the left. The former Kingsway tram subway passes under and along the road here. The bus is on a 243 service bound for Waterloo Station.",
          "alt": "Holborn tube station Holborn is on both the Central and Piccadilly Lines, and the Piccadilly Line station was opened in 1906. In 1933 the station was substantially modernized including the opening of the Central Line station, which replaced the British Museum station about 250 metres away to the west. \nThis is the west entrance to the station in Kingsway. There is a north entrance in High Holborn round to the left. The former Kingsway tram subway passes under and along the road here. The bus is on a 243 service bound for Waterloo Station.",
